    {
      "id": "b2",
      "function": "problem",
      "scene_type": "rv_cutaway",
      "spoken": "Normally the spark ignites the charge, and a flame runs through the chamber. Ahead of it sits the still unburned mixture, the end gas. The growing flame squeezes it and makes it hotter. The spark sits in the middle, so the edges burn last.",
